cheepicus@hotmail.com wrote:
>* Nerfed Reflection
>Instead of each reflection-giving item granting perfect reflection,
>items would have individual probabilities of reflecting attacks, and
>each item gets a chance to reflect any one attack. Rough shot at
>numbers: artifacts (generally) 90%, AoR 95%, SDSM 99%, SoR 99.9%,
>being-a-SD 100%. Breath weapons harder to reflect.

Probabilistic reflection is worthless as soon as a death ray or
disintegration blast gets past it. Try this instead:

Reflection only *mostly* reflects the ray.
* Damage-dealing rays (e.g. MM, fire) do 1/n of their normal damage, and
  the reflected ray loses 1/n of its "warhead strength". 
* Instakill rays (divine-wrath lightning, black dragon breath, death
  rays) for which you do not have the relevant resistance do damage
  equal to 1/n of your maximum hit points instead of killing you, and
  anyone hit by a reflection-bounce of such a ray will only take damage
  equal to (n-k)/n of their hit points (where 'k' is the number of times
  the beam has been reflected by Reflection).
* Inventory-damaging rays (e.g. fire) have an extra 1/n check
  applied to their chance of damaging your possessions.

Adjust 'n' as necessary to secure good game balance. For the moment,
retain the current behaviour regarding gaze attacks.
